        "id": "i",
        "text": "Which claim correctly distinguishes the triples?",
        "marks": 1,
        "options": [
          {
            "id": "A",
            "text": "$(5, 12, 13)$ is primitive because $\\gcd(5,12,13)=1$; $(10, 24, 26)$ is a scale of that triple by $2$."
          },
          {
            "id": "B",
            "text": "Call $(10, 24, 26)$ a non-primitive triple label only, with no common-factor check."
          },
          {
            "id": "C",
            "text": "Scaling every entry by $2$ is what creates the primitive triple $(5, 12, 13)$ from $(10, 24, 26)$."
          }
        ]
      },
